<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20606" root="سم" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمْسَمٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمٌّ</span>, first sentence. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is also an
epithet, of which only the fem., with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, is mentioned: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمَامٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمْسَمٌ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمْسَامٌ</span></b> ,
(M,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّمْسَمُ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّمْسَامُ</span></b> , (K, TA,) [the latter
erroneously written in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السِّمام</span>,]) <i>The wolf;</i>
(M, K;) because of his lightness, or activity, or
agility: (M:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّمْسَمُ</span> signifies <i>the wolf that is
small in the body.</i> (M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّمْسَمُ</span> <i>The
fox;</i> (S, M, K;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمْسَمٌ</span> [without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ال</span>],
(M,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السُّمَاسِمُ</span></b> . (K.)

